<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Marinid Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1244 CE – 1465 CE · capital Fez</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Zenata Berber dynasty that replaced the Almohads in Morocco and made Fez a great centre of learning, adorned with celebrated madrasas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Banu Marin were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanata-berbers">Zenata</a> nomads from the steppes of the eastern Moroccan frontier. As the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> weakened they raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco's</a> plains, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meknes">Meknes</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in 1248, and in 1269 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-yusuf-yaqub-ibn-abd-al-haqq">Abu Yusuf Yaqub</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a>, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> rule. Their emergence as a regional power is often dated to the 1240s.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a>, founding the royal city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fes-el-jdid">Fes el-Jdid</a> in 1276 and building <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a> such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bou-inania-madrasa-fez">Bou Inania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-attarine-madrasa">al-Attarine</a> to train <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maliki-school">Maliki</a> scholars. They intervened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> to support the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/emirate-of-granada">Emirate of Granada</a>. Abu al-Hasan conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zayyanid-kingdom-of-tlemcen">Zayyanid Kingdom of Tlemcen</a> and briefly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, but lost at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rio-salado">Rio Salado</a> in 1340. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a> wrote his travels for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-inan-faris">Abu Inan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-inan-faris">Abu Inan</a>'s death in 1358 real power passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">viziers</a>, notably the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/wattasid-sultanate">Wattasids</a>. Portugal took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> in 1415. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-haqq-ii">Abd al-Haqq II</a> was killed in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> uprising in 1465, and the Wattasid Sultanate eventually succeeded.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/marinid-sultanate.jpg" alt="Marinid Sultanate" width="320" height="191"><figcaption>Image: Askelaadden (minor modifications by R Prazeres) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marinids_Zayyanids_and_Hafsids_c1360.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1244 CE – 1465 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fez</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abu Yusuf Yaqub, Abu al-Hasan Ali, Abu Inan Faris</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Maliki)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a>, <a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Marinids, Banu Marin, Marinid dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1354&amp;focus=marinid-sultanate" aria-label="Marinid Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4553 944 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Marinid Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps